This portion of the AI capstone is to recreate Turing's Bombe to serve as a comparison
to our machine learning model's accuracy and speed

Quick notes on how the bombe works
designed by Alan Turing and Gordon Welchman
used the enigma machines biggest weakness in order to solve what the settings were
that being that the encrypted letter would never be itself 
ex) if you click x you could get any other letter in the alphabet except x

Basic principles of how the bombe works
1) uses known words (cribs)  that you know are in the encrypted text
2) kind of brute forces it until it reaches settings that do work

How to actually use the files
1) Run the Bombe Text Processor file so that it converts a txt file 
to a processed text file that removes all commas, periods, replaces numbers with characters
ex) 3 gets turned to 3
but also removes all of the spaces too

2) after you have the processed text file run the  Processed text to encrypted text file
This is basically the enigma machine part where it converts that processed file into a 
encrypted text file, here you set the initial rotor positions 

Currently this part has working rotors but does not have the plugboard implemented yet

3) Then run whatever is the most recent version of the Bombe file
It'll have a small built in enigma machine, its importnat since if you run it without it
its like opening a lock when there is no lock

After its done it'll print out its results and its estimated initial rotor positions

TLDR
1) run text processor with the text file you want to process
2) Run the processed text to encrypted text file using previous file as its input file
3) run bombe 
